Firstly, thanks to Robin et. al. for running the tourney - I always
seem to play better in November.
This year fragmites made three ascensions, all (personally) noteworthy.
The first was a neutral dwarven valk, chosen as something fairly easy
to go with the grue challenge. She found an early magic lamp, recovered
the sinister device, and then neglected to deactivate it, eventually
bringing an active grue generator to the demi-god's bar. Vortices
become very scary if you play like that (though wands of light help if
you see them coming). Thankfully the Plane of Air is lit and the orb
with tele control is an excellent escape mechanism when a vortex sneaks
up on you round a corner in Gehemmon. Other than that, a normal enough
valk. No reflection until Perseus, no MR before the castle wand, a
gremlin stealing my protection and no amulets before Vlad's were merely
inconvient. There was a close shave on the Astral where a smart role
monster threw a !Blind at me; I'm wearing a helm of telepathy, so start
swinging the hammer at them. Next thing I see is the sword that would
have decapited me bouncing off my AoLS (destroying it in the process).
A wand of teleport sent that problem to the other side of the map, and
ascension soon followed.
The second ascension was a lawful monk - my first ascended monk and
with 7 conducts to boot. (weaponless, polyself and poly object-less,
vegan hence veggy, arti-wishless and genocide-less. Also, by my
standard practice, Elbereth-less). Vegan was not so bad as my god gave
me telepathy while I was making spellbook prayers. This monk finished
off the grue challenge (another magic lamp provided light thoughout). I
killed Vlad before Master Kaan, the normal cause of my monk deaths. I
used the fireproof water-walking boots trick and an HP prayer, and a
wand of teleport pointed at myself before finally beating him up with
my bare hands then finishing up with +6 shiriken (the RNG was being
very generous with them; I had a pile of 25 odd. After Master Kaan, the
rest seemed pretty easy (though I saw an awful lot of Orcus town).
Ascension 2, and a birdie (no bells).
A few more pathetic deaths later, and a chaotic elven priest took the
stage (I was still hoping for five races). Priest was another first for
my ascensions - I haven't played them much and my earlier attempts had
all died before the quest. Stealth helped the quest. GoP, a robe and
lots of levels from the wraiths gave Stormbringer a good amount of
hitting power; while still allowing very decent spell-casting. No
particular alarms or excursions after the quest and castle wand and
three tourney ascensions.
After that, my stupidity outweighed my luck (on new moon days, seeing
chickatrices before you've met a lizard should be a cause for concern
and dropping all your food for blessed ?ID purposes is fine, but do
remember to pick it up again afterwards) so three was the total, not
bad but a long way from Marvin.

Hoping to see you all on Devnull next year,

